            <ArticleTitle>Efficacy of palliative radiation therapy for symptomatic rectal cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>258-261</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0167-8140(16)34307-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.radonc.2016.06.023</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>99 patients with symptomatic locally advanced rectal cancer who were treated with palliative radiation alone were reviewed. Dose-fractionation ranged from 18 to 54Gy. Response rate ranged from 62.5 to 86.7%, with a median response duration ranging 4.2-5.4months. Median survival was 6.9months. Using a BED cut-off of 39Gy10, no dose-response relationship was found.</AbstractText>
